# ── Recorded transition, 2026-10-13 — merge of v0.28.0 phase 4 (training on
#    Vertex AI, Std.Ai.Serve, Std.Ai.Cloud.Google) with phase 5 ──
#   80 of 84 rows measured; 03-tea-external, 05-mux-server, 08-notes-app and
#   13-skyshop are carried forward (SKY_LIVE_TESTS=skip): they import no
#   Std.Ai module, and installing their FFI surfaces would take the disk under
#   its 60 GB floor. Two new rows: 74-ai-cloud 1589 and sky-bundled/ai-cloud
#   634. Nine rows rise, each because the program now compiles more Std.Ai
#   code, not because existing code got less typed: 73-ai-train 1007 -> 1462,
#   sky-bundled/ai-train 872 -> 1360, sky-bundled/ai 552 -> 731,
#   71-ai-registry 790 -> 907, 72-ai-support-desk 434 -> 514, 70-ai-synthetic
#   408 -> 479, 75-ai-everywhere 855 -> 926, 68-ai-dataset 489 -> 500,
#   sky-bundled/console 182 -> 183. The new code is the Vertex backend in
#   Std.Ai.Train (cloud settings, plan, launch, watch, mirror, cleanup), all of
#   Std.Ai.Cloud.Google, Store's generation-guarded object operations,
#   Registry's companions and pointer objects, three Failure codes and the
#   Endpoint's Google auth. In 73-ai-train's emitted Go the narrowing sites by
#   module are Std.Ai.Train 473, Std.Ai.Store 134, Std.Ai.Registry 131,
#   Std.Ai.Cloud.Google 127 and Std.Ai.Failure 88; by kind, rt.Field on an
#   erased record (128), ADT payload reads (`_subj.Fields`, R6, about 140) and
#   Coerce at call and pattern sites. No single kernel dominates, so no §5.3
#   twin closes a large share; the largest twin candidates are
#   `AsListT(String.split …)` (29) and `AsBool(String.isEmpty …)` (10). Not
#   traced site by site.
# ── Recorded transition, 2026-10-13 — phase 4 rises, reduced and cited ──
#   83 of 86 rows measured; 05-mux-server, 08-notes-app and 13-skyshop are
#   carried forward (SKY_LIVE_TESTS=skip, no generated FFI surface, and
#   installing it would take the disk under its 60 GB floor). No row rises;
#   37 fall. Two levers:
#   * R5 (lower.rs `kernel_call`, the `kernel_typed_return_twin` branch),
#     lever §5.3: `String.split` / `isEmpty` / `lines` over proven strings go
#     to `rt.String_splitT` / `String_isEmptyT` / `String_linesT`, and
#     `System.getenvOr`, `Secret.reveal`, `Crypto.sha256` to `..T` twins that
#     assert the erased kernel's one result type. §1: the kernel's result has
#     one Go type and a `Some` parameter is used only when the argument
#     already lowers to it, so both shapes are known at emit time.
#     runtime-go/rt/kernel_twins_test.go checks each twin against its erased
#     kernel.
#   * R6 (lower.rs `narrow_ctor_subject` / `narrow_erased`), lever §5.2 with
#     the record resolution of goty.rs (`record_fieldsets`): the payloads of
#     Std.Ai.Failure's 27 constructors, Std.Ai.Train's `Event`, `Job` and
#     `BaseModel` and Std.Ai.Dataset's `Issue` are named records. A match
#     then reads a payload with one narrowing instead of one per field. §1:
#     the payload's shape is known; `SkyADT.Fields[i]` stays `any` by the
#     stdlib-ADT contract (§4.5), so one narrowing remains per read.
#   The gate that goes red if either regresses is this one (narrow is
#   fail-on-increase on every Std.Ai row); the Std.Ai suites
#   (scripts/sky-suites.sh Std_Ai, 14 suites) prove the semantics.
#   Rows against their value before phase 4 (15944613d):
#     68-ai-dataset 489 -> 431 and sky-bundled/console 182 -> 180: below.
#     70-ai-synthetic 408 -> 419 (+11), 71-ai-registry 790 -> 825 (+35),
#     72-ai-support-desk 434 -> 442 (+8), 75-ai-everywhere 855 -> 868 (+13),
#     sky-bundled/ai 552 -> 651 (+99), 73-ai-train 1007 -> 1292 (+285),
#     sky-bundled/ai-train 872 -> 1186 (+314).
#   Cause, per row: each rise is smaller than the sites in functions that
#   did not exist before phase 4 (counted per emitted Go function against
#   the 15944613d stdlib): 70 has 43 such sites, 71 has 139, 72 has 82, 75
#   has 43, sky-bundled/ai 126, 73 440, sky-bundled/ai-train 459. The code
#   that existed before phase 4 now carries fewer sites than it did. The new
#   code is reachable in every one of these programs, so dead-code
#   elimination cannot drop it, and no dispatch restructuring would:
#   - Std.Ai.Cloud.Google's token code (43 to 51 sites per row) is reached
#     from every `Endpoint`: `Endpoint.endpoint` holds `Google.idToken`
#     (Endpoint.sky, the default record), and `SKY_AI_<SLOT>_AUTH=google`
#     turns it on at run time (runtime-go/rt/ai_endpoint.go, `cfg.auth ==
#     "google"`).
#   - Std.Ai.Store's GCS and S3 object operations are chosen by the store
#     URL's scheme at run time (`Store.fromUrl`), and the registry's
#     companion and pointer objects are written by every `register` /
#     `promote`.
#   - Std.Ai.Train's Vertex backend is chosen at run time by
#     `SKY_AI_TRAIN_BACKEND=vertex` (runtime-go/rt/ai_train.go,
#     `aiTrainResolveBackend`), which overrides `withBackend` and detection
#     by design: a program built for a local backend runs on Vertex AI by an
#     environment variable, so every training program links it.
#   The remaining sites in this code are R2 (`eta_narrow`, the JSON decoder
#   callbacks: already the closed form), R6 reads of stdlib ADTs (§4.5), R10
#   / R11 `rt.Field` on open rows (policy floor, §4.6) and R5 returns of
#   kernels with no one-type twin. New rows: 74-ai-cloud 1589 -> 1414 and
#   sky-bundled/ai-cloud 634 -> 540, measured, not limited.
# ── Recorded transition, 2026-10-14 — the P4 live-run commits
#    (d83301526..d6bd6b493), rises closed ──
#   84 of 86 rows measured; 05-mux-server and 08-notes-app are carried forward
#   (SKY_LIVE_TESTS=skip, no generated FFI surface). No row rises; 5 fall.
#   The 17 commits raised four rows: 73-ai-train 1292 -> 1302, 74-ai-cloud
#   1414 -> 1431, sky-bundled/ai-cloud 540 -> 554, sky-bundled/ai-train
#   1186 -> 1196. The compiler was not the cause: the d83301526 Sky sources
#   (Train, Serve, Cloud.Google, ai-cloud Main) measure the golden exactly.
#   Per emitted Go function, the new tokens were: Train.watchCloud +6
#   (`Task.map2` into a tuple callback, R1 via `box_func_value`, and
#   `Maybe.withDefault (Maybe.map …)` over the previous cloud.json, R12 + R11
#   `rt.Field`), Train.readCloudFile +2 (a nested `JsonD.map2` tuple),
#   Train.cloudRelaunch +2 (two new Task callbacks), Google.remoteHas +7 (new),
#   Google.validLabel +3 (now reached in sky-bundled/ai-cloud through
#   `allLabels`), Serve.dockerfileWith +2 (new) and ai-cloud teardownVerb +2.
#   Closed by restructuring the new code so the shapes are known at emit time:
#   * watchCloud reads the previous file with `case` on the typed
#     `Maybe CloudFile` (R8, lever §5.2, `.JustValue` typed read) and binds
#     `now` and the file with two nested `andThen`s, not a `map2` tuple: +0.
#   * readCloudFile decodes with one `JsonD.map5` over a `map3` triple: +0.
#   * Google.validLabel uses `Regex.match`, a typed kernel twin (R5, lever
#     §5.3), not `List.all` over `String.toList` (R12, and R2 for the
#     `rune` narrowing in its callback): -3 in every row that reaches it.
#   * Google.pathOf and regionOf take the first `String.split` piece with a
#     cons pattern on the typed `[]string` instead of `List.head` +
#     `Maybe.withDefault` (R12 via R1): -2 each.
#   * remoteHas takes the endpoint artifactExists already read (pure
#     `serviceBaseFor`), matches the decoded mode with `case`, and fetches the
#     token with one `andThen` (a `Secret` callback narrows nothing): 7 -> 3
#     over remoteHas and manifestReachable.
#   * Serve.dockerfileWith and ai-cloud teardownVerb build their text with
#     `String.join ""` over a typed `List.map` (`String_joinT`, R5, §5.3)
#     instead of joining a `::` list (an erased `List_cons` return); ai-cloud
#     `text` and `bucketOf` use `case` instead of `Maybe.withDefault` (R12).
#   Tokens left in the new code, each offset by the falls above:
#   cloudRelaunch +1 (the launch step now writes cloud.json inside the step,
#   so it gains one `\launched -> … |> Task.map (\_ -> launched)` pair, less
#   the removed `Task.succeed () |> Task.andThen`), remoteHas +3 (the `\resp`
#   and `\r` Task callbacks and the `JsonD.decodeString` result) and
#   teardownVerb +1 (`List.all` over the `::` label list, R12). The callback
#   tokens are R1 at `box_func_value` (lower.rs): a typed Sky lambda boxed
#   into the erased `func(any) any` slot of the Task kernels
#   (`rt.AnyTaskAndThen` / `rt.Task_map`, run by the Task trampoline). By §1
#   both shapes are known, so they are closeable only by typed Task kernel
#   twins (§5.3), which do not exist; every existing `andThen` pays the same.
#   Rows now: 73-ai-train 1286, sky-bundled/ai-train 1180, 74-ai-cloud 1411,
#   sky-bundled/ai-cloud 537. 13-skyshop 1190 -> 1188 (measured with its FFI
#   surface): its two `String.split` sites (`Std.Css.rawProp`,
#   `Lib.Auth.adminEmails`) now reach the `rt.String_splitT` twin added by
#   the previous transition (R5, §5.3); the row was carried forward then.
#   Std.Ai suites (scripts/sky-suites.sh Ai, 14 suites), ai_cloud_train_flow
#   and ai_serve_flow prove the behaviour is unchanged.
# ── Recorded transition, 2026-10-17 — Std.Ai.Device engine settings
#    (Device.withThreads / withGpuLayers) ──
#   All 86 rows measured. One row rises: 75-ai-everywhere 846 -> 849 (+3);
#   every other row unchanged. Cause (2), new code: three new wire fields,
#   the offer's `threads` and `gpuLayers` and a backend's `gpu`
#   (Std.Ai.Device offerDecoder +2, infoDecoder +1, counted per emitted Go
#   function against HEAD's Device.sky). Each is one argument of the JSON
#   decoder's callback (R2, `eta_narrow` at the decoder's erased slot: the
#   closed form, doc 14 §5.1), as every existing field of those decoders
#   pays. The decision itself added none: `fits` reads the typed backend list
#   through a recursion (`holds`) instead of a `List.any` lambda (R12), which
#   offsets the GPU check, and `reasonFor` reuses `holds` rather than a new
#   comparison (an erased `==` on the Backend ADT, R5, measured +1 when it was
#   a helper of its own). The defaults decode with `JsonD.oneOf` instead of
#   `Maybe.withDefault` (R12, measured +4 before).
#
# ── Recorded transition, 2026-10-17 — Std.Ai.Trace across the lifecycle,
#    local drafts and named adapters, strict AI settings; then the closeable
#    narrowings in that code removed ──
#   All 86 rows measured. The first commit of this transition raised eight AI
#   rows by +242 (70 +2, 71 +48, 72 +2, 73 +51, 74 +36, 75 +51,
#   sky-bundled/ai +3, sky-bundled/ai-train +49). A Judge found closeable
#   narrowings (R1, R5, R12) in that rise; this re-bless removes them. The
#   eight rows now sum to 7054 (7305 before this re-bless, 7063 before the
#   transition), and the golden to 17344 (17783 before). Every row fell or
#   held; none rose. Two causes:
#   * Lowering (doc 14 §1, R1, identity): a partially applied def in a func
#     slot whose param is the def's own Go param type declared that param
#     `any` and narrowed it back (`trainOn`: `rt.Coerce[Adapter_R](_p1)` with
#     `_p1` already `Adapter_R`). `lower.rs::make_partial` now declares it at
#     the type when the slot names the same type. Corpus-wide: 07-todo-cli
#     -4, 19-skyforum -8, 62-app-notes -12, … (regression test
#     `lower/tests/partial_identity_param.rs`).
#   * Source, in the functions this transition added or changed:
#     `addProgressLine` reads the checkpoint with a `case`, not `Maybe.map
#     .checkpoint` (R12/R11 `rt.Field`); `upsertStep` builds with `[ x ] ++
#     rest` (typed `rt.List_appendT`), not `::` (R5 `rt.List_cons`);
#     `cloudStatus` (`moneyOrZero`), `factsOf` (`orText`), `rate`,
#     `measuredOf`, `Endpoint.withLocal` (`orUnset`), `Eval.runCase`,
#     `Eval.okResult` and `Trace.callRow` use a `case` for `Maybe.withDefault`
#     / `Maybe.map` (R12); `Eval.callModel` uses a `case` for `Result.map`
#     (R12); `Eval.scoreCall` / `okResult` / `errResult` take a monomorphic
#     `CaseInfo`, not the polymorphic `Suite input` / `Case input` (R12 and a
#     second R6 destructure); `Device.fits` / `holds` / `reasonFor` compare a
#     Backend by name (`sameBackend`, `listed`, `unsupportedWhy`), not the
#     erased `==` (R5 `rt.Eq`) or `List.member` (R12); `requestValue`,
#     `turnValue` and `toolSpecValue` are annotated (R12 `rt.AsListT[any]`).
#   What remains in those functions, by origin:
#   * R6, stdlib ADT payloads (§4.5, blocked by the runtime contract):
#     `Error.withMessage` 2, `Durable.conn` 3 (the `Ctx` payload),
#     `Endpoint.withLocal` 1 (`Config`), `addProgressLine` 2 (`Event`),
#     `Provider.measure` / `measureTools` 3 each (`Provider`'s payloads),
#     `Eval.runCase` 9 (the `Suite` payload, field by field).
#   * NOT floor, OPEN (closing each is a compiler change across the corpus):
#     - the erased callback slot of a Task or JSON-decoder kernel
#       (`Task.andThen` / `map` / `map2` / `onError`, `JsonD.mapN`): the
#       `widen` adapter narrows the kernel's `any` argument. `insertRow` 2,
#       `setup` 1, `traceCost` 2, `traceLines` 1, `withTraceTables` 2,
#       `trainOn` 3, `cloudStatus` 12, `timed` 1, `timedWith` 1,
#       `finishTimed` 2, `measure` / `measureTools` 1 each, `judgeAnswered`
#       3, `scoreCall` 2, `runCase` 4. Lever: typed kernel entry points
#       (§5.3; `rt.Task_mapT` exists and the lowerer does not route to it).
#     - R12, the polymorphic `timed` / `timedWith` (`Timing a`): the record's
#       `rt.Coerce[Timing_R[any]]` in `measure` / `measureTools` (2 each) and
#       `timedWith`'s `attempt` result 1. Lever §5.5. Monomorphic copies were
#       measured and cost MORE (+13 on 75), because of the next item.
#     - R1, a parametric record alias at a concrete type
#       (`Measured ChatResponse`) lowers to an anonymous struct in a signature
#       and to `Measured_R[any]` in a literal (`goty.rs`
#       `select_record_candidate` refutes a template that holds the param
#       inside a type constructor), so each crossing narrows field by field:
#       `Eval.callModel` 7.
#     - R5, kernel returns: `rate` 1 (float `/` is `rt.Div`), `cloudStatus` 1
#       (`JsonD.decodeString`'s result).
#
# Ratcheted down on feat/std-ai-lifecycle (decreases only; measured by
# `xtask coerce-floor` on this tree):
#   - R5, lever 5.3: float `/` over two `Float` operands lowers to the typed
#     `rt.DivF(float64, float64) float64` instead of `rt.Div` (no boxing, no
#     narrowing of the result): 26-ui-showcase -4, 35-composite-generics -6,
#     37 -2, 38 -2, apps/fieldbook -5, sky-bundled/ai -2, sky-bundled/console -2.
#   - R6, doc 14 4.5: `Std.Codec.Codec`'s payload is the named record
#     `CodecPayload`, so a match on a codec narrows once instead of once per
#     field. This also pays for the codec's new `sch` field (the JSON Schema
#     description behind `Codec.jsonSchema`): every program that destructures
#     a codec drops by 8 (07, 08, 12, 16, 17, 18, 27, 36, 52, 55, 62,
#     apps/dispatch, apps/ledger), the AI programs by 3 to 27.
#   72-ai-support-desk rose 435 -> 660 (+225) with its new typed tool,
#   structured answer and durable assistant (it now links Std.Durable and
#   Std.Ai.Agent). Raised by hand on the user's decision (2026-10-25): no new
